    "checks": [
      {"id":"statement","passed":true,"finding":"The payload states exactly the three source conditions in Stacks-compatible terms and separately states the zero-differential cohomology equivalence."},
      {"id":"one_iff_two","passed":true,"finding":"Triangulatedness, the per-morphism kernel/cokernel normal-form criterion, and the abelian-category definition prove both directions; in normal form the coimage-to-image map is the identity on the middle summand."},
      {"id":"two_implies_three","passed":true,"finding":"For a monomorphism between degree-zero complexes, split normal form gives a generalized inverse aba=a; homotopies are zero in degree zero, and monicity yields ba=1, so each short exact sequence splits."},
      {"id":"split_complex_decomposition","passed":true,"finding":"Splitting the cycle and boundary short exact sequences gives X^n=B^n_X direct-sum H^n(X) direct-sum B^{n+1}_X with differential (b,h,c) mapped to (c,0,0)."},
      {"id":"contractible_summand","passed":true,"finding":"For C_X^n=B^n_X direct-sum B^{n+1}_X, the stated s^n(b,c)=(0,b) satisfies d s+s d=1 in the cochain convention."},
      {"id":"hstar_functor_and_full_faithfulness","passed":true,"finding":"Cohomology is homotopy invariant, the chosen inclusion and projection induce identities, and maps between zero-differential complexes are determined by cohomology; the displayed Hom-set inverse therefore proves full faithfulness."},
      {"id":"essential_surjectivity_and_abelianity","passed":true,"finding":"Every complex is isomorphic in K(A) to its cohomology complex, while zero-differential complexes identify with Gr(A), which is abelian; hence K(A) is abelian."},
